meta {
  name: 02_ResourcePolicies
  seq: 2
}

docs {
  Scenario: The rules of one or more app policies can be read in one request

    Given the app ttd/authz-bruno-testapp1 has a stored policy
    When the policies are requested for that app, the response is 200 with
    the actions, the role grants and the minimum authentication level
    And a list mixing a known app, an unknown app and an entry without an
    app is answered entry by entry, with an errorResponse on the failures
    When the body is not a list of lists, the response is 400

  POST /authorization/api/v1/policies/GetPolicies takes a list where each
  entry identifies one app as a list of attribute matches (urn:altinn:org
  and urn:altinn:app). The response has one entry per request entry, in the
  same order. A lookup that fails for one entry does not fail the request:
  that entry carries errorResponse and the status stays 200.
}
